📅 Day 31 – Console-Based JDBC Mini Project (Part 2)

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session continued the development of the console-based JDBC mini project. The mentor guided us in implementing the core functionalities required for interacting with the database through the console application.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Implementing Database Operations

The focus of the session was on writing code to perform basic database operations within the project.

Operations implemented:

Insert Records → Adding new entries into the database table

Display Records → Retrieving and showing stored data from the database

These operations allowed the console application to interact directly with the database.

2️⃣ Integrating SQL Queries with Java

The mentor demonstrated how SQL queries can be integrated into the Java application using JDBC components such as:

Connection → Establish database connection

PreparedStatement → Execute SQL queries

ResultSet → Retrieve and display database results

🔹 Practical Implementation

During the practice session, I worked on:

Integrating database queries into the console-based project

Testing the application by inserting records into the database

Displaying stored data through the console interface

Verifying that database connectivity was working correctly

This step improved the functionality of the application and ensured smooth interaction between the Java program and the database.